<article class="env-lemma" id="0A3V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A3V">Lemma <span data-tag="0A3V">29.29.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of finite type with $Y$ quasi-compact. Then the dimension of the fibres of $f$ is bounded. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/02FZ" data-tag="02FZ">29.29.4</a> the set $U_ n \subset X$ of points where the dimension of the fibre is $\leq n$ is open. Since $f$ is of finite type, every point is contained in some $U_ n$ (because the dimension of a finite type algebra over a field is finite). Since $Y$ is quasi-compact and $f$ is of finite type, we see that $X$ is quasi-compact. Hence $X = U_ n$ for some $n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>